Body:
Yeah, the only way I got it working with local ollama was to edit ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json and to set it to (for my specific local setup).

```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",

  "model": "ollama/qwen3.6:35b-a3b",

  "provider": {
    "ollama": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "name": "Ollama",

      "options": {
        "baseURL": "http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1"
      },

      "models": {
        "qwen3.6:35b-a3b": {
          "name": "qwen3.6:35b-a3b",
          "tools": true,
          "reasoning": true
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

especially for beginners/new people to this tool, it would be helpful if this would be integrated configurable natively
